TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-1. Setup: what goes where', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 1, 'summary': 'Do this first: the new files and how it behaves.', 'content': '<p>Step 1 of 6. Your <code>view.py</code> and <code>process.py</code> stay as they are. Add these new files to the portfel app. The two <code>__init__.py</code> files are empty — without them Django does not see the command.</p>\n<h3>Layout</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-plaintext">portfel/\n    daily.py            ← new\n    management/\n        __init__.py     ← empty\n        commands/\n            __init__.py ← empty\n            build_portfel.py\n</code></pre>\n<p>The two systemd files (steps 4 and 5) do not go into the project: they go to <code>/etc/systemd/system/</code>.</p>\n<h3>How it behaves</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>08:00</b> — builds the previous working day (on Monday: Friday).</li>\n<li>The database returned 0 rows (not updated yet) → the run fails, nothing is saved, <b>09:00, 10:00, 12:00, 14:00</b> try again.</li>\n<li>After a success the later runs only print «already done».</li>\n<li>Still nothing at 14:00 → «last try for today — giving up». That day has no portfel.</li>\n<li>Raw file saved but processing failed → the next run only processes, no second query.</li>\n<li>Saturday and Sunday: no runs.</li>\n</ul>\n'})

TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-2. daily.py', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 2, 'summary': 'The same steps as portfel_get + portfel_process, but without a user: query → raw → all + svod. Writes .tmp first, svod last.', 'content': '<p>Step 2 of 6. Save as <code>portfel/daily.py</code>.</p>\n<h3>daily.py</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-python">"""\nBuilds the portfel files for one day WITHOUT a user — the same steps as the views\nportfel_get + portfel_process, but with no request, no session and no messages.\n\nUsed by the command `python manage.py build_portfel`, which the systemd timer runs\non working days at 08:00, 09:00, 10:00, 12:00 and 14:00 (see management/commands/build_portfel.py).\n\nFiles are written as "&lt;name&gt;.tmp" first and renamed at the end, so a page opened while\nthe job is still writing never sees a half-written file. The svod file is written LAST:\nif it exists, the day is finished.\n"""\nimport datetime\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport pyarrow as pa\nimport pyarrow.parquet as pq\n\nfrom functions import common_functions\nfrom . import queries\nfrom .process import process_portfel_best\n\nBASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\nportfel_input_folder = BASE_DIR / "datasets" / "portfel" / "input"\nportfel_svod_folder = BASE_DIR / "datasets" / "portfel" / "svod"\nportfel_all_folder = BASE_DIR / "datasets" / "portfel" / "all"\nutils_path = BASE_DIR / "utils" / "useforauto.xlsx"\n\n\nclass NotReadyYet(Exception):\n    """The database returned no rows for this day — it is not updated yet."""\n\n\ndef previous_working_day(today=None):\n    """Yesterday; on Monday it is Friday (and on Saturday/Sunday also Friday)."""\n    today = today or datetime.date.today()\n    days_back = {0: 3, 6: 2, 5: 1}.get(today.weekday(), 1)   # Mon → Fri, Sun → Fri, Sat → Fri\n    return today - datetime.timedelta(days=days_back)\n\n\ndef raw_path(day):\n    return portfel_input_folder / f"raw_{day}.parquet"\n\n\ndef svod_path(day):\n    return portfel_svod_folder / f"svod_{day}.parquet"\n\n\ndef all_path(day):\n    return portfel_all_folder / f"all_{day}.parquet"\n\n\ndef is_ready(day):\n    return svod_path(day).exists()\n\n\ndef fetch_raw(day, log=print):\n    """Query Oracle for the day and save raw_&lt;day&gt;.parquet. Raises NotReadyYet on 0 rows."""\n    os.makedirs(portfel_input_folder, exist_ok=True)\n    final = raw_path(day)\n    tmp = final.with_name(final.name + ".tmp")\n    conn = None\n    pq_writer = None\n    rows = 0\n    try:\n        conn = common_functions.get_oracle_connection()\n        batch_generator = conn.fetch_df_batches(\n            queries.best_portfel_script,\n            parameters={\'pdate\': day},\n            size=100000,\n        )\n        for odf in batch_generator:\n            arrow_table = pa.table(odf)\n            if pq_writer is None and arrow_table.num_rows == 0:\n                break\n            if pq_writer is None:\n                pq_writer = pq.ParquetWriter(tmp, arrow_table.schema)\n            pq_writer.write_table(arrow_table)\n            rows += arrow_table.num_rows\n            log(f"  fetched {rows:,} rows")\n    finally:\n        if pq_writer:\n            pq_writer.close()\n        if conn:\n            conn.close()\n\n    if rows == 0:\n        tmp.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n        raise NotReadyYet(f"no rows for {day} — the database is not updated yet")\n    os.replace(tmp, final)\n    log(f"  raw saved: {final.name} ({rows:,} rows)")\n\n\ndef process_day(day, log=print):\n    """raw_&lt;day&gt;.parquet → all_&lt;day&gt;.parquet + svod_&lt;day&gt;.parquet (svod last)."""\n    os.makedirs(portfel_svod_folder, exist_ok=True)\n    os.makedirs(portfel_all_folder, exist_ok=True)\n    df_raw = pd.read_parquet(raw_path(day))\n    svod_df, all_df = process_portfel_best(df_raw, utils_path)\n\n    try:\n        final = all_path(day)\n        tmp = final.with_name(final.name + ".tmp")\n        all_df.to_parquet(tmp)\n        os.replace(tmp, final)\n        log(f"  all saved: {final.name}")\n    except Exception as e:\n        log(f"  all file is not saved: {e}")          # same as the view: svod is what matters\n\n    final = svod_path(day)\n    tmp = final.with_name(final.name + ".tmp")\n    svod_df.to_parquet(tmp)\n    os.replace(tmp, final)\n    log(f"  svod saved: {final.name}")\n\n\ndef build_day(day, force=False, log=print):\n    """Everything for one day. Returns False if it was already done, True if built now."""\n    if is_ready(day) and not force:\n        return False\n    if force or not raw_path(day).exists():\n        fetch_raw(day, log=log)\n    else:\n        log("  raw file already exists, only processing")\n    process_day(day, log=log)\n    return True\n</code></pre>\n'})

TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-3. build_portfel.py', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 3, 'summary': 'The command: previous working day (Monday → Friday); already built → nothing; database not updated → fails, the next run tries again.', 'content': '<p>Step 3 of 6. Save as <code>portfel/management/commands/build_portfel.py</code>.</p>\n<h3>build_portfel.py</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-python">"""\nBuilds the portfel for the previous working day (on Monday: Friday), without a user.\n\nThe systemd timer runs it on working days at 08:00, 09:00, 10:00, 12:00 and 14:00:\n  * day already built     → it does nothing (so after a success the later runs are free);\n  * database not updated  → it fails, and the next run tries again;\n  * after the 14:00 run   → nobody tries any more; that day simply has no portfel.\n\nBy hand:\n    python manage.py build_portfel                     # previous working day\n    python manage.py build_portfel --date 2026-10-23   # a chosen day\n    python manage.py build_portfel --date 2026-10-23 --force   # query and process again\n"""\nimport datetime\nimport traceback\n\nfrom django.core.management.base import BaseCommand, CommandError\n\nfrom portfel import daily\n\nLAST_TRY_HOUR = 14\n\n\nclass Command(BaseCommand):\n    help = "Build the portfel files for the previous working day."\n\n    def add_arguments(self, p):\n        p.add_argument("--date", type=datetime.date.fromisoformat, default=None,\n                       help="YYYY-MM-DD; default: previous working day")\n        p.add_argument("--force", action="store_true",\n                       help="query and process again even if the files exist")\n\n    def handle(self, *a, **o):\n        day = o["date"] or daily.previous_working_day()\n        now = datetime.datetime.now()\n        self.stdout.write(f"{now:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} portfel for {day}")\n\n        def log(msg):\n            self.stdout.write(str(msg))\n            self.stdout.flush()\n\n        try:\n            built = daily.build_day(day, force=o["force"], log=log)\n        except Exception as e:\n            if not isinstance(e, daily.NotReadyYet):\n                log(traceback.format_exc())\n            if o["date"] is None and now.hour &gt;= LAST_TRY_HOUR:\n                raise CommandError(f"{day}: {e}. That was the last try for today — giving up.")\n            raise CommandError(f"{day}: {e}. Will try again at the next run.")\n\n        if built:\n            self.stdout.write(self.style.SUCCESS(f"{day}: done"))\n        else:\n            self.stdout.write(f"{day}: already done, nothing to do")\n</code></pre>\n'})

TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-4. portfel.service', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 4, 'summary': 'What the timer runs. Copy User= and Environment lines from gunicorn.service.', 'content': '<p>Step 4 of 6. Save as <code>/etc/systemd/system/portfel.service</code>.</p>\n<h3>portfel.service</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-ini"># /etc/systemd/system/portfel.service\n# Copy User= and every Environment=/EnvironmentFile= line from gunicorn.service,\n# so the job reaches Oracle exactly the way the website does.\n[Unit]\nDescription=Portfel: build the previous working day\n\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nUser=www-data\nWorkingDirectory=/var/www/dashboard/dashboard\nExecStart=/var/www/dashboard/delta/bin/python manage.py build_portfel\n# a stuck query is killed before the next try starts\nTimeoutStartSec=50min\n</code></pre>\n'})

TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-5. portfel.timer', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 5, 'summary': 'When: working days at 08, 09, 10, 12 and 14 Tashkent time. After 14:00 nobody tries again.', 'content': '<p>Step 5 of 6. Save as <code>/etc/systemd/system/portfel.timer</code>.</p>\n<h3>portfel.timer</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-ini"># /etc/systemd/system/portfel.timer\n# Working days at 08, 09, 10, 12 and 14 Tashkent time. A run after a success does\n# nothing; after 14:00 nobody tries again — that day has no portfel.\n[Unit]\nDescription=Portfel tries on working days\n\n[Timer]\nOnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 08,09,10,12,14:00:00 Asia/Tashkent\nPersistent=true\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=timers.target\n</code></pre>\n'})

TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'PFA-6. Turn it on', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 6, 'summary': 'Test by hand, enable the timer, read its log.', 'content': '<p>Step 6 of 6. First a test by hand, on a date you know has data:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">cd /var/www/dashboard/dashboard &amp;&amp; source ../delta/bin/activate\npython manage.py build_portfel --date 2026-10-23\n</code></pre>\n<p>Then switch the timer on:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">sudo systemctl daemon-reload\nsudo systemctl enable --now portfel.timer\nsystemctl list-timers | grep portfel     # when the next try is\njournalctl -u portfel -n 50              # what the tries printed\nsudo systemctl start portfel.service     # one try right now\n</code></pre>\n<p>After changing either systemd file: <code>sudo systemctl daemon-reload</code> again. After <code>git pull</code> nothing else is needed — the next run uses the new code (no gunicorn restart for the timer).</p>\n<p>⚠️ «Not updated yet» means the query returned 0 rows. If the database can be <i>half</i> loaded at 08:00, that half day is saved and not retried — then it needs a better «is the load finished?» check.</p>\n'})
